sub:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-suzukii-turing-wavelength-s0> pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-suzukii-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-suzukii-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Drosophila suzukii Turing onset wavelength at 2.046 µm (0 Ma, detail scale) — MorphoEval overall 87.2/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Pass 2. Eigenvector-initialized mode growth matches analytical sigma(k) with Pearson r = 0.9999999995 and RMSE = 4.16e-4 on the real-eigenvalue band. Diffusivity sweep r = 0.997 and is monotonic. Equal-diffusion and subobscura std(u) are 1e-15, drawn flat on the focal color scale. A stripe seed on the 24.552 µm window locks to spacing 2.046 µm (CV 0.056). The noise-seeded field remains a labyrinth (CV 0.37, KS 0.63). Specimen Otsu metrics differ from their priors. lambda_c = 2.046e-6 m, age 0 Ma. Fastest-growing wavelength is 2.116 µm, slightly longer than onset, as expected just above threshold (margin > 1 at diffusion ratio 12.6). Overall 87.2/100 (faithfulness 86.1, reproducibility 89.8); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 0c76d15d; environment: . Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 88, Morphological realism / specimen match 82, Parameter expressivity 90, Morphometric validation 88, Source and data traceability 91, Code-to-model traceability 88, Reproducibility package 90. Output judged: docs/media/drosophila_suzukii_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-suzukii-turing-wavelength-s0.py at 0c76d15d, image/png, 562769 B, 1584×984 px, artifact_sha256 e240d3ff629f62b8628ad36760770d1c8f961a5e7ca4c4daa4fa8196d85b386a (sha256 e240d3ff629f62b8628ad36760770d1c8f961a5e7ca4c4daa4fa8196d85b386a), spec_fingerprint 8f4a40558dfdd1a363ec347c2232dbab086e21c6d2b0baf5b5a36feb603bb029. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 8f4a40558dfdd1a363ec347c2232dbab086e21c6d2b0baf5b5a36feb603bb029; artifact_sha256: e240d3ff629f62b8628ad36760770d1c8f961a5e7ca4c4daa4fa8196d85b386a; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/drosophila_suzukii_turing_wavelength_s0/drosophila_suzukii_specimen.jpg=a4180479fce43c90..., datasets/drosophila_suzukii_turing_wavelength_s0/drosophila_suzukii_turing_wavelength_s0_reference.json=6dcb8c0b6f42ebaf...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-27-drosophila-suzukii-turing-wavelength-s0-audit. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Male D. suzukii has an apical wing spot; the female has a serrated ovipositor (Atallah 2014). | Spot presence in the suzukii–biarmipes clade is a yellow cis-regulatory gain (Gompel 2005; Prud'homme 2006; Koshikawa 2020). | A two-species reaction-diffusion system selects a finite onset wavenumber k_c (Turing 1952).; reconstructed_in_script: Schnakenberg a=0.037, b=1.284, D_v/D_u=12.6, D_u solved so the onset wavelength is 2.046 µm. | Subobscura uses a=0.52, b=0.18 so f_u = -17/35 and the Turing band is absent. | Takahashii keeps the kinetics and multiplies both diffusivities by 1.44, so lambda_c = 2.4552 µm (10 waves in the same window instead of 12). | The periodic window quantizes a stripe seed onto lambda_c = 2.046 µm even though the fastest linear wavelength is 2.116 µm.; transfer_boundary: 2.046 µm is the campaign detail-scale assignment, not a measured granule spacing. | The McEvey plate (960×640, 1 mm bar) anchors the animal. It does not resolve the carrier.; does_not_claim: That yellow or ebony kinetics are Schnakenberg reactions, or that D_u and D_v were measured. | That D. takahashii's pigment wavelength has been measured at 2.455 µm. | That subobscura → suzukii → takahashii is a fossil ancestor chain. All three are Holocene (0 Ma); the order is the comparative chronoseries.." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
        pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: D_u, D_v and the takahashii factor 1.44 are calibrated hypotheses, not measured diffusivities.",
            "remediation needed: Noise-seeded labyrinth spacing KS remains 0.63. The stripe seed shows the onset mode is selectable; it does not make the nonlinear labyrinth periodic.",
            "remediation needed: Still one assessor. A second provider has not scored this audit.",
            "remediation needed: Still one plate. Abdominal trough count 7 versus a tergite prior of 6 is an ROI method on n = 1, not a population.",
            "remediation needed: The McEvey plate does not resolve 2.046 µm. Organism-level Otsu numbers are not a carrier measurement." ;
        pk:hasScore "0.872"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Grok 4.7 (Cursor cloud agent, builder-assessor; no second provider on this run)" ;
        dct:identifier "grok-4.7" ;
        prov:actedOnBehalfOf <https://orcid.org/0009-0007-4948-9192> .
}

